From: Frank Sorenson <sorenson@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:55:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] cifs: fix loff_t underflow in cifs_remap_file_range() when
 len == 0
Git-commit: 6c322f5cf7476ded7a9a20f7be72462065a03c68
References: bsc#1280950 CVE-2026-89640
Patch-mainline: v7.3-rc1

With len == 0 (clone to EOF), the effective length is computed as:

    len = src_inode->i_size - off;

If off > i_size, this is a negative loff_t, corrupting the ByteCount
in the FSCTL_DUPLICATE_EXTENTS_TO_FILE request and inverting the range
in filemap_write_and_wait_range().  The existing off >= i_size check
fires only after the ioctl has already been sent.

Snapshot i_size_read() once for both the bounds check and the length
calculation, eliminating the TOCTOU and 32-bit torn-read risk.  Reject
off > src_size with -EINVAL.  Treat off == src_size as a no-op,
consistent with __generic_remap_file_range_prep().

Fixes: 04b38d601239 ("vfs: pull btrfs clone API to vfs layer")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Frank Sorenson <sorenson@redhat.com>
Reviewed-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.org>
Signed-off-by: Henrique Carvalho <henrique.carvalho@suse.com>

[ hc: this tree predates the VFS remap_file_range conversion; the
  equivalent is the older .clone_file_range callback
  cifs_clone_file_range(), where len is already a u64 rather than a
  loff_t. There is no "unlock" label here, so the two new early-exit
  branches call unlock_two_nondirectories() inline before jumping to
  the existing "out:" label. ]
---
 fs/cifs/cifsfs.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/cifs/cifsfs.c b/fs/cifs/cifsfs.c
index 2073b29ff9698..7ecd70efdfea8 100644
--- a/fs/cifs/cifsfs.c
+++ b/fs/cifs/cifsfs.c
@@ -1162,7 +1162,20 @@ static int cifs_clone_file_range(struct file *src_file, loff_t off,
 	lock_two_nondirectories(target_inode, src_inode);

-	if (len == 0)
-		len = src_inode->i_size - off;
+	if (len == 0) {
+		loff_t src_size = i_size_read(src_inode);
+
+		if (off > src_size) {
+			rc = -EINVAL;
+			unlock_two_nondirectories(src_inode, target_inode);
+			goto out;
+		}
+		len = src_size - off;
+		if (!len) {
+			rc = 0;
+			unlock_two_nondirectories(src_inode, target_inode);
+			goto out;
+		}
+	}

 	cifs_dbg(FYI, "about to flush pages\n");
 	/* should we flush first and last page first */
-- 
